# APP-09 clean-clone validation: without this file, a Windows clone
# (Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true) checks every tracked text
# file out with CRLF line endings. Two concrete failures that caused:
#
# 1. backend/docker/entrypoint.sh -- COPY . . bakes the CRLF version into
#    the (Linux) backend image, so its shebang becomes "#!/bin/sh\r". The
#    container can't resolve that interpreter and crash-loops with
#    "exec docker/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory". This is the
#    one that actually breaks `docker compose up --build` on a clean
#    Windows clone.
# 2. Every other tracked text file (.ts, .md, .yml, ...) also checks out as
#    CRLF, so Biome's `format`/lint check -- which expects LF, matching how
#    the rest of the repo was authored -- flags them after every checkout,
#    `git am`, etc., even when nothing actually changed.
#
# Forcing LF on checkout for every text file, and explicitly for shell
# scripts, fixes both regardless of a given contributor's local
# core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
